WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.613
The teal bar runs from nine thirty to ten

00:00:03.573 --> 00:00:07.652
Those thirty minutes are preparation time They are not

00:00:07.771 --> 00:00:10.771
spare space simply because they appear before the decision

00:00:10.771 --> 00:00:11.323
meeting

00:00:12.193 --> 00:00:15.259
Now compare the amber request from nine forty-five to

00:00:15.325 --> 00:00:19.061
ten fifteen It takes the last fifteen minutes of

00:00:19.127 --> 00:00:22.114
preparation and the first fifteen minutes of the decision

00:00:22.114 --> 00:00:22.653
meeting

00:00:23.527 --> 00:00:26.830
Keep the supplier slot labelled requested until the approval

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:30.751
is verified Show both conflicts when asking for a

00:00:30.803 --> 00:00:34.106
decision instead of hiding one behind a calendar change
